  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Round-trip swap: base \\xe2\\x86\\x92 bridge (split OK) \\xe2\\x86\\x92 base (split OK) in one\\natomic invocation.\\n\\nFunds are pulled from `user` and the final `base_token` balance is\\nreturned to `user`. The contract does not retain funds after\\nexecution.\\n\\n# Parameters\\n\\n- `leg_out`: sub-routes from `base_token` to `bridge_token`. Each\\n`SubRoute.amount_in` is an absolute base-token input; they **must**\\nsum to `amount_in`.\\n- `leg_back`: sub-routes from `bridge_token` to `base_token`. Each\\n`SubRoute.amount_in` is a **positive weight** (quoted bridge amounts\\nare fine). After `leg_out` produces actual bridge total `o1`, weights\\nare rescaled so executed inputs sum **exactly** to `o1` (last\\nsub-route receives the remainder). Callers do **not** need to know\\n`o1` at submit time.\\n- `min_amount_out`: minimum total `base_token` returned (principal +\\nprofit floor)\\n\\n# Integrator note\\n\\nSame `SubRoute` type for both legs \\xe2\\x80\\x94 no extra fields. Semantics of\\n`amount_in` differ by leg: absolute on `leg_out`, proportional weight\\non `leg_back`.",
      "name": "round_trip_swap",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "user",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "base_token",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "bridge_token",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "amount_in",
          "type_": "i128"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "leg_out",
          "type_": {
            "vec": {
              "element_type": {
                "udt": {
                  "name": "SubRoute"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "leg_back",
          "type_": {
            "vec": {
              "element_type": {
                "udt": {
                  "name": "SubRoute"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "min_amount_out",
          "type_": "i128"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        "i128"
      ]
    }
  },
